Goal 1: Improve incident resolution
Within the next 12 months, I will improve my ability to manage and resolve complex Salesforce support issues by leading at least one major incident or problem investigation each quarter. I will focus on faster root cause analysis, clearer communication with users and stakeholders, and stronger coordination with development and infrastructure teams. I will document recurring issues, identify patterns, and help reduce repeat incidents through permanent fixes or process improvements. Success will be measured by shorter resolution times, fewer escalations, and better feedback from internal teams and business users.
Goal 2: Strengthen support quality
Over the next 12 months, I will strengthen support quality by improving how I triage tickets, assess impact, and prioritise work based on business urgency and system risk. I will aim to resolve a higher percentage of support requests within agreed service timelines while maintaining accurate notes and clear handovers. I will also contribute to better knowledge articles and troubleshooting guides so common issues can be handled more efficiently. Success will be measured through improved SLA performance, fewer repeat queries, and smoother support experience for end users.
Goal 3: Build technical support capability
Within the next 12 months, I will build stronger technical support capability by deepening my knowledge of Salesforce configuration, integrations, release processes, and monitoring tools. I will use this knowledge to assist with troubleshooting, support releases, and reduce dependency on others for day-to-day issues. I will also support junior team members by sharing practical guidance and helping them understand common support scenarios. Success will be measured by improved confidence in handling complex cases, better team productivity, and more effective support across Salesforce-related incidents and requests.

